# Foundation Uno — publication hygiene.
#
# At U00 there is no application and no build output. These rules exist to keep the
# PUBLIC repository free of private authority, task scratch, credentials and build
# products that later stages will produce. An ignore rule screens a path from Git; it
# never deletes, moves or rewrites a file.

# --- Owner-authorized work order: PRIVATE, never published -------------------
# Private Owner authority — exclude this single file, never the whole WIP directory.
# The governing work order lives at the canonical WIP path and is read-only to
# implementation agents. It must never appear in `git ls-files` or in a pushed commit.
/.documents/WIP/workorder-active.md
# DO NOT add `/.documents/WIP/` here. That would screen the entire directory and the
# three public `plan-*.md` slots must stay trackable. Only the ACTIVE file is private.
# A root-level `/workorder-active.md` is never a valid order, so it stays screened too.
/workorder-active.md

# --- Agent task scratch and disposable local evidence ----------------------
/.temp/

# --- Node.js / pnpm / Next.js build products ------------------------------
/node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/
/.next/
/out/
/build/
/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
/.vercel/

# --- Task logs, transient files and local diagnostics ---------------------
*.log
/tmp/
*.tmp

# --- Credentials, keys and environment -----------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.keystore

# --- OS and editor noise -------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
